  "prefLabel": "He-W 746.02 Establishing Certification Periods",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 746.02 Establishing Certification Periods.\n\n(a) Thirty-six months certification shall be allowed for households in which:\n\n(1) There is no earned income; and\n\n(2) All adult household members are age 65 or older or disabled as defined in 7 CFR 271.2.\n\n(b) In accordance with 7 CFR 273.10(f)(3), up to 6 months certification shall be allowed for households in which:\n\n(1) There is earned income; or\n\n(2) At least one adult household member is not age 65 or older or disabled as defined in 7 CFR 271.2.\n\n(c) In accordance with 7 CFR 273.10(f)(3), a certification period of less than 6 months shall be allowed for households where the household’s situation is unstable.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for He-W 700) #5133, eff 5-2-91; ss by #6507, INTERIM, eff 5-1-97, EXPIRES: 8-29-97; ss by #6549, eff 8-1-97; ss by #7282, eff 6-1-00; amd by #7510, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9174, eff 6-7-08; ss by #11141, eff 7-22-16; ss by #14655, eff 7-17-26, EXPIRES: 7-17-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w700.html"
